# Help: Block drivers no other fragment builds
#
# The PC floppy driver, Micron's PCIe SSD driver, ATA over Ethernet and
# the Ceph RADOS block device, which selects the Ceph library. With
# storage/block-devices.config, storage/block-test-devices.config,
# storage/ublk.config, storage/rnbd.config, storage/rnull.config,
# mem/zram.config and virt/xen.config this builds every driver under
# drivers/block an x86_64 guest can. BLK_DEV_FD needs a PC floppy
# controller, which only x86 has, behind ISA DMA, whose default y an
# allnoconfig-based merge drops; its prompt needs EXPERT.
#
# Layer builtin/storage/block-drivers.config to build them in (=y).
# See: drivers/block/Kconfig

#
# Inlined prerequisites (x86_64)
#
CONFIG_EXPERT=y
CONFIG_ISA_DMA_API=y

#
# Block drivers
#
CONFIG_BLK_DEV_FD=m
CONFIG_BLK_DEV_PCIESSD_MTIP32XX=m
CONFIG_ATA_OVER_ETH=m
CONFIG_BLK_DEV_RBD=m
